# 6. Core Problem Statement

The current Review Commits analysis can produce false positives, especially for minor releases.

The key question is:

> How can Release Tracker determine the actual ancestry/source of a release branch and choose the correct commit-analysis strategy?

For example:

### Expected minor-release flow

```text
master
  |
  +---- Major Release
           |
           +---- Minor Release
                    |
                    +---- cherry-picked fixes
```

### Actual minor-release flow sometimes observed

```text
master
  |
  +---- Minor Release
```

These two cases require different analysis logic.

